/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (A public sector firm will seek to maximise social welfare/utility/achieve allocative efficiency \(1\) Government funds public services to deliver high levels of consumer satisfaction to the population \(1\) This means they will consider private and external costs and benefits \(1\), unlike a private sector firm which will only care about profit \(1\). Public sector firms aim to keep prices as low/quality as high as possible for consumers \(1\))
